{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)-7brty","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)-7czhh","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:tableName:bundle:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/body"]},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/obfuscationCharacter","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter"]},{"anchor":"Enumerations","generated":true,"title":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/Length","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/Status"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/View-Implementations","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/View-Implementations"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/oudscomponents\/oudspincodeinput"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSPinCodeInput"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Layouts","anchor":"Layouts","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component can be rendered as two different layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"outlined"}]},{"text":" layout: A minimalist input with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages, e.g. when inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"in a header (search field), or in a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not outlined","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" (default): An input with a subtle background fill and visible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component provides 3 layouts for the input: 4 boxes, 6 boxes or 8 boxes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A helper text can be used to support text to convey additional information about the input field, such as how it will be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus."}]},{"anchor":"Error-status","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Error status"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Error status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or expected formatting."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border, error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input (mandatory)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This state helps users quickly identify and correct mistakes by explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The input remains editable, encouraging users to revise their input without starting over."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The error state must be triggered by an explicit validation (submission, API response), and not in real time with each keystroke."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This can occur either because the entered code does not match the expected code, because the user entered an expired or already used code,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or finally if the maximum number of attempts has been exceeded."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Specific-design-guidelines","level":2,"text":"Specific design guidelines"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the context of a PIN code input, in addition to the input’s “Error” UI rendering, it is essential to also include an “Alert” component"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(also in its “Error” status) in the interface."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Particular-cases","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Particular cases"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" component supports autofill feature of values like OTP code."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example if the user receives a message with inside a code the system can extract, the keyboard can suggest to the user to fill it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits fits the component, it will be filled."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits are longer, they will be truncated."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits are shorter, they will be filled, letting other fields empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The copy\/paste feature is also available and has the same behavior."}]},{"anchor":"Technical-considerations","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Technical considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For some cases, on phones screens or with 8 boxes in iPhone, you may need to use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScrollView"},{"type":"text","text":" to embed the component and let user move it."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScrollView(.horizontal) {","    OUDSPinCodeInput($value,","                     length: .eight,","                     helperText: \"Enter your secret code sent to your phone\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note also the exposed ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"value"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"text":" will be updated when all digits are written.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]},{"anchor":"Accessibility-considerations","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Accessibility considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The content of the fields is vocalized by Voice Over; the placeholders (defined in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/obfuscationCharacter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not vocalized to let users know what they wrote."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component gets only numeric values, not letters or symbols, only numbers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Depending on the component configuration, autofocus can still be used when the component appears, and focus is moved to the next field as digits are entered."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example if Voice Over is enavled, the autoficus is disabled."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component and its digit fields are vocalized with internal wording."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using the error status, provide a clear, concise error message explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(for example: "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“The code you entered is invalid. Try again.”"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use helper text to communicate additional guidance (for example: "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Check the 6‑digit code sent by SMS”"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), and keep this text short so it remains easy to vocalize"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and understand."}]},{"anchor":"Rich-text","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Rich text"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"No other text styles should be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users."}]},{"text":"Code samples","anchor":"Code-samples","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","code":["    \/\/ The value with the code","    @State private var pinCode: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ By default, the PIN code input displays only 6 boxes","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode)","","    \/\/ It can have also up 4 or 8 boxes, with an helper text","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .eight, helperText: \"Enter your 8 secret digits\")","","    \/\/ The component can be used in error contexts","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .six, status: .error(message: \"The OTP code you entered is not correct\"))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Design-documentation","text":"Design documentation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-pin-code-input"}]},{"text":"Themes rendering","anchor":"Themes-rendering","type":"heading","level":2},{"text":"Orange","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Orange"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Orange"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Orange-Compact","level":3,"text":"Orange Compact"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_OrangeCompact","type":"image"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Sosh","level":3,"text":"Sosh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Sosh","type":"image"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Wireframe","level":3,"text":"Wireframe"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Wireframe","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Version","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3.0 (Figma component design version)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"Since","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.4.0"}]}]}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSPinCodeInput"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"title":"OUDSPinCodeInput","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSPinCodeInput"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","platforms":[{"beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"15.0"},{"beta":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0"}],"externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents16OUDSPinCodeInputV"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"PIN code input is a UI element that allows to capture short, fixed-length numeric codes, typically for authentication or confirmation purposes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as a four, six or eight-digit personal identification number (PIN)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"PIN code input is presented as a series of individual input fields or boxes, each representing a single digit, to enhance readability and encourage accurate input,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while supporting smooth keyboard navigation and secured input masking if needed."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"references":{"component_pinCodeInput_Orange":{"alt":"A PIN code input component in light and dark modes with Orange theme","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/OUDSComponents\/component_pinCodeInput_Orange.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"type":"image","identifier